 1230|       |      // instantiation where it cannot, this function is noexcept (see the
 1231|       |      // signature) and the handler is unreachable -- GCC reports exactly that as
 1232|       |      // -Wterminate, since it sees a `throw` inside a noexcept function. Saying
 1233|       |      // so with `if constexpr` compiles the handler only where it can run,
 1234|       |      // which is what the code already meant.
